  "worked_solution": "Notice that the $2$nd column contains three zeros. So, using Laplace expansion along the $2$nd column, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(P) & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 & 2 \\\\ -3 & 0 & 8 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 7 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(-2)\\cdot (-1)^{4+2}|\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 2 \\\\ -3 & 8 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 2 \\\\ -3 & 8 & 0\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, notice that the $3$rd column of the $3\\times 3$ determinant contains two zeros. So, using Laplace expansion along the $3$rd column, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(P) & =-2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 2 \\\\ -3 & 8 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(-2)\\cdot (2\\cdot (-1)^{2+3}|\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 \\\\ -3 & 8\\end{aligned}|) \\\\  & =4\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 \\\\ -3 & 8\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =4(8-(-12)) \\\\  & =4\\cdot 20 \\\\  & =80.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
